.TH GETSOCKNAME 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getsockname \- get a socket's local address
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int getsockname(int descriptor, struct sockaddr* address, socklen_t* length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes the local address to a writable buffer. On entry length gives the
buffer capacity; on return it gives the actual address length, which can
exceed capacity if truncated.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getpeername (3crunch),
.BR getsockname (2)
